  "rule": "per class, over both arches: a class's UNROLLED form is admissible when its stack is at most STACK_BUDGET_B = 14,000 B (#613's gradient-family budget) on sm_86 and on gfx1200 and its compile finishes within COMPILE_BUDGET_S = 300 s on both. If any class is inadmissible, the low-stack form is gated by an la + lb floor, LOWSTACK_MIN_LSUM = the smallest la + lb with an inadmissible class: every class below it must be admissible (so stays unrolled, its text unchanged), every class at or above it is gated. Every low-stack unit must itself be within both budgets on both arches; where one is not, the form is changed, never the budget. With no inadmissible class, gjab keeps one form (LOWSTACK_MIN_LSUM None)",
